meta {
  name: Upload Attachment Without fileName
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/storage/upload
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(notes/sample-attachment.txt)
  fileSize: 59
  folder: notes/{{torgId}}
}

assert {
  res.body.statusCode: eq 400
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.data.error: eq fileName is required
}

docs {
  Negative case for "Upload Attachment" (BUG-715): the same upload with the `fileName` form field left
  out. The stored key and content type are built from `fileName`, so the upload is refused: the resource
  answers 400 with `{"error":"fileName is required"}`, and the API wrapper turns that into HTTP 200 with
  the envelope `{"data":{"error":"fileName is required"},"message":"{error=fileName is required}",
  "statusCode":400,"success":false}` (like every other error here, check the body). Nothing is stored. Before the fix this came back as a 500.

  An upload that fails inside storage now returns only "Failed to upload file" in the 500 body (no
  internal detail); that is not provoked here.
}
